slide 1: Urology — Medical Education | medical students • 5 learning cards | AI-assisted draft — not clinically approved. Faculty must verify every claim and reference.
slide 2: Which finding indicates acute urinary retention? | Answer / teaching points | Painful inability to void with a palpable bladder. | G-001 • basic • unreviewed
slide 3: Which finding indicates acute urinary retention in an adult? | Answer / teaching points | Painful inability to void with a palpable bladder. | G-002 • basic • unreviewed
slide 4: What imaging is typically first line for suspected renal colic? | Answer / teaching points | Non-contrast CT or ultrasound depending on local pathway. | G-003 • basic • unreviewed
slide 5: List the components of a focused scrotal examination. | Answer / teaching points | Inspection, palpation, transillumination, cremasteric reflex. | G-004 • basic • unreviewed
slide 6: Describe the role of prostate specific antigen testing in the assessment of older men | Answer / teaching points | Digital rectal examination plus informed PSA discussion. | G-006 • basic • unreviewed
